A||N||5||Matt85_GT||Help fiero start and stall||||1||
Z||000000||Matt85_GT||04-06-2000||10:34 PM||||I am new to the list and have and 85 GT (V6). The problem I have is that it will fire right up then quit after about 3 seconds of running.  I have replaced the wires, cap, distributor, rotor,and fuel pump.  It has good fuel pressure and holds pressure.  I am going mad try to figure it out.  I looked at the past posts and saw people with similar problems, but I haven't seen the cure yet.  Please help I am ready to kill fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Ed||04-06-2000||11:14 PM||||Check your fuel pump fuse.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||BAM-BAM||04-06-2000||11:31 PM||||   Matt, I also have an 85GT with a similar problem. Does your  car do that the first time you try to star it, then start and stay running  the second time? Does it start and stay running after it is warmed up? If so, quit taking my car at night:P. Just kidding. I have replaced all the sensors, TPS, IAC, EGR<BR>tube, EGR regulator, wires, plugs, cap, rotor, O2sensor, and it still does that. This weekend I am going to replace the air charge sensor in the air cleaner(back left).<BR>And, I am going to replace the fuel filter. I'm not sure how old mine is, but I'm sure it's old. I will let you know if there is any improvement. I did notice some improvement after replacing the IAC valve.<P> Late, BAM-BAM  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000003||Phil||04-07-2000||07:07 AM||||Sounds like you could have a bad oil pressure sender. The computer starts the fuel pump (for about 3 sec. I think)then a switch in the oil pressure sender keeps it running. No fuel no run. Does the pressure gage work? If you believe you have oil pressure try jumping  the wires (forget the colors check your Haynes).||||reg||1
Z||000004||JohnnyK||04-07-2000||09:29 AM||||Mine will do the exact same thing (Start and quit the first time, but run on the second try).. I heard it could be the coil? Does anyone know before I replace it?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||lennyb4||04-07-2000||09:57 AM||||I had the same problem. Turned out my  throttle position sensor was bad. When it first started it would slam the butterfly closed stalling the car. The second time it would work properly. If you have a digital multitester you can check the voltage on the sensor its self. Check the haynes manual for the exact specifications, if not i can find it for you.||||reg||2
